# Crash integration sharding

Preserve the optimized crash workflow:

- one Ubuntu job runs the complete crash suite;
- Windows snapshot crash tests run in a dedicated shard;
- Windows install crash tests run in a dedicated shard;
- Windows update crash tests run in a dedicated shard;
- `fail-fast` remains false;
- `CGO_ENABLED=0` remains explicit;
- crash tests retain the crash build tag;
- each crash test must belong to exactly one Windows shard;
- no crash test may be omitted;
- no crash test may match multiple shards;
- adding an unassigned crash test must fail CI;
- use stable test-name prefixes rather than fragile broad expressions;
- upload or report shard durations;
- compare the longest Windows shard against the previous approximately seven-minute sequential job;
- never reduce duration by deleting, skipping, or weakening crash tests.
<!-- MEW-CRASH-SHARDING_END -->
